$x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x+1.$ For those points, the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x+1\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that some points in our set lie *on* the line. We include these points by changing the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\ge -x+1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge -x+1}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/state.json" "file_sha256" "422f3aad3a54d06a86a8149634494fbfb38639ec50b964bf61f967a9cd2caf2b"} {"question" "q-181970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25eaf4ef883a9b1d1c4ea99d87a63ae5d7238e0a15ae283d35abbc4373c79042"} {"question" "q-181970" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/state.json" "file_sha256" "422f3aad3a54d06a86a8149634494fbfb38639ec50b964bf61f967a9cd2caf2b"} {"question" "q-181970" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "N"] ["math" "R"] ["math" "Z"] ["math" "{N}^{2}"] ["math" "{R}^{2}"] ["math" "{Z}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/state.json" "file_sha256" "422f3aad3a54d06a86a8149634494fbfb38639ec50b964bf61f967a9cd2caf2b"} {"question" "q-181970" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{Z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Co