state.json" "file_sha256" "422f3aad3a54d06a86a8149634494fbfb38639ec50b964bf61f967a9cd2caf2b"} {"question" "q-182024" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/state.json" "file_sha256" "422f3aad3a54d06a86a8149634494fbfb38639ec50b964bf61f967a9cd2caf2b"} {"question" "q-182024" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "<"] ["math" ">"] ["math" "\\ge "] ["math" "\\le "] ["math" "\\ne "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/state.json" "file_sha256" "422f3aad3a54d06a86a8149634494fbfb38639ec50b964bf61f967a9cd2caf2b"} {"question" "q-182024" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ge "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/state.json" "file_sha256" "422f3aad3a54d06a86a8149634494fbfb38639ec50b964bf61f967a9cd2caf2b"} {"question" "q-181678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/0f95f6b259237816a5a3da041452cfd9458f0852b1ae717a044738b6f310ab5d.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,3\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,2x+3}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/state.json" "file_sha256" "422f3aad3a54d06a86a8149634494fbfb38639ec50b964bf61f967a9cd2caf2b"} {"question" "q-181678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=3$ and *below* the line $y=2x+3.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>3,\\,y<2x+3.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n3<y<2x+3.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the lines $y=3$ and $y=2x+3$ since the boundaries are included in the set (the lines are solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbols above as follows:\n\n$$\n3\\le y\\le 2x+3\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,3\\le y\\le 2x+3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/state.json" "file_sha256" "422f3aad3a54d06a86a8149634494fbfb38639ec50b964bf61f967a9cd2caf2b"} {"question" "q-181678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "25eaf4ef883a9b1d1c4ea99d87a63ae5d7238e0a15ae283d35abbc4373c79042"} {"question" "q-181678" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/state.json" "file_sha256" "422f3aad3a54d06a86a8149634494fbfb38639ec50b964bf61f967a9cd2caf2b"} {"question" "q-181678" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "C"] ["math" "N"] ["math" "R"] ["math" "{C}^{2}"] ["math" "{R}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/state.json" "file_sha256" "422f3aad3a54d06a86a8149634494fbfb38639ec50b964bf61f967a9cd2caf2b"} {"question" "q-181678" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/c